Tuesday
Today was a little exhausting due to catching a cold (I shall never escape
sickness lol) but it was still a good day. We had my district counsel
meeting and we had to ride trains for like 30 minutes to get there; we
shared a few stories and did a couple mogis to practice our teaching. After
we were done, we went to eat at a restaurant all together; I got some
shrimp Tempura and it was really good. On the way home I bought a couple of
donuts for some reason lol. The first had anko (sweet bean paste) inside
and I really enjoyed it. I'm glad, because I have heard a lot of foreigners
do not lol. When we got back, we did studies for a while then went to the
Fukuda=E2=80=99s home to have a meal and teach a short spiritual message. B=
rother
and sister Fukuda are like 70 or 80 and they are super nice; our dinner was
very traditionally Japanese and consisted of crushed up doritos in a bowl
with various taco materials =F0=9F=98=82 Definitely not what I was expectin=
g. Was
very tasty though~

Wednesday
Today Elder Berg and I taught the beginner Eikaiwa class which was very
fun. A lot of the class was pretty sidetracked but it was probably still
good English practice for the students lol. Afterwards we played Badminton
(we meaning everyone besides me because of my foot lol) but I did get to
spectate and draw, which was fun. Also did a little experimenting with my
new camera.

Thursday
Tsuji san
Basketball

Friday
On Friday I don't remember a lot from the day, we probably taught a lesson
or something but I'm writing this on P-Day so I'm unsure =F0=9F=98=82 Howev=
er, Friday
night I do remember we ate Hamburger steak (basically just Hamburger
patties lol) with cheese and rice and ketchup and it was amazing. I could
only eat a couple of them, but it was great =F0=9F=8D=94 This was for a YSA=
 activity,
and afterwards people just kind of sat around and talked. I sat with a dude
named Yuuhi and talked for like an hour, he's super cool. He loves eating
all kinds of bugs (cooked of course) and i get the feelinb we are gonna eat
some together soon =F0=9F=91=80 his favorite things are also camping and Ha=
rry Potter
for some reason. He loves SciFi but his favorite movies and books are Harry
Potter it cracks me up =F0=9F=98=82

Saturday
Saturday we had a gyoza making party with the YSA that could come which
were literally 3 people besides me, my companion, and or roomates, so
that's 4 missionaries and 3 YSA lol. It took us like 2 hours to buy and
prepare the gyoza as well as another hour of talking and eating. It was
amazing. I ate probably 15 gyoza and I had to hold back so more people
could eat lol.

Sunday
We went to a members son=E2=80=99s baptism
Bike get (got a bike and I am in pain from the seat)
Meal at the Ikawas

Monday
Train
Zone Conference (will write more about this next week if I can, Lotta stuff
happened)
Hirakata

Tuesday (This week's Pday cause of Zone conference)
Today was a crazy Pday. We went to the other area=E2=80=99s church to call =
family
and meet up with our district (some of them anyways) to go to the MR. Donut
museum and get some chicken with a member named Shingo. It was pretty fun
and the donuts at the end were fire. There was one donut (I did not buy)
that said =E2=80=9CMexican Meat=E2=80=9D on it and I really don't understan=
d what that
means, but it's a little frightening =F0=9F=98=82 after our lengthy excursi=
on (after
which I talked with Shingo-San for like an hour) Elder Sonomura and I met
up with someone I found on HelloTalk named Monica, and we talked and ate
for an hour or two, was super fun. She speaks Pretty solid English but
mostly spoke Japanese cause she said she was shy lol. We ate some
Okonomiyaki, which was really good and I'm pretty sure my mom would have
loved the one I ordered.

Sorry a couple days were very briefly described, But I'm pretty short on
time particularly due to how long it took us to get home from eating food
with Monica-San (Pray for Elder Sonomura to be led spiritually but mostly
directionally =F0=9F=98=82=F0=9F=98=85)

Lobe you guys!!

-Elder Killian

Spiritual message
Very brief today, but where ever you're at in life, I'd invite you to
simply write down 3 things you're grateful for. If you can write down at
least 1 thing a night you're grateful for, you might be surprised by the
end of the week, or month =F0=9F=98=81=F0=9F=98=81

